.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead dep list" 1  "bead dep list " 
.SH NAME
bead dep list \- List dependency edges for an issue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead dep list\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show every dependency edge touching one issue, in both directions.
.PP
\*(AqBlocked by\*(Aq lists blockers this issue depends on; \*(Aqblocking\*(Aq lists dependents
that depend on this issue as their blocker. Each edge reports its kind and
whether the other issue in the edge is finished (base status \*(Aqclosed\*(Aq).
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead dep list ID                  # Human\-readable, both directions
  bead dep list ID \-\-json           # One JSON object: {id, blocked_by, blocking}
.PP
EXIT CODES:
  0  success, even when the issue has no dependencies
  3  the issue does not exist
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Issue ID
